BLINK PTHREAD BUILD FINDING (sandcastle/portabox): adding emscripten -pthread did NOT flip Blink's HAVE_FORK/HAVE_THREADS. Root cause: Blink's ./configure uses autoconf-style probes that COMPILE+RUN a test binary to detect fork()/pthreads; under emconfigure the test compiles to wasm which can't be executed natively, so every runtime probe reports 'no' (fork... no, pthreads... no, PTHREAD_PROCESS_SHARED... no) regardless of -pthread. The flag DID reach the compiler (wasm 266KB->807KB, pthread runtime linked). ALSO: -pthread build broke the Node smoke test with 'ReferenceError: self is not defined' (threaded glue assumes worker global). Fix path: force -DHAVE_FORK -DHAVE_THREADS etc via CPPFLAGS to bypass the unrunnable probe, AND fix smoke test for worker env (or test in browser). Single-threaded build (sha 80e9953392, 266KB) remains the known-good fallback and is live in webix main. f159e22 pthread build is broken (not committed - smoke failed).